          "en": "But he didn't despise himself, and things didn't turn out as he had imagined. He probably planned to take what he could and leave, but now he found himself committed to following a dream. He knew Daisy was extraordinary, but he didn't realize how extraordinary a \"nice\" girl could be. She vanished into her rich house, into her rich, full life, leaving Gatsby with nothing. He felt married to her, and that was all.",
